# EtSymbol Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtSymbol` is a styled box component for displaying currency symbols, icons, dates, or text labels. It provides:

- **Multiple sizes**: small (24px), medium (36px), large (48px)
- **Multiple shapes**: rounded (border radius), sharp (square corners)
- **Compound component pattern**: `EtSymbol.Currency`, `EtSymbol.Icon`, `EtSymbol.Date`, `EtSymbol.Text` subcomponents
- **Gradient overlay**: Always-on gradient overlay matching the design system

**Does NOT handle:**

- Navigation or press interactions (wrap in Pressable if needed)
- Image-based symbols (use EtAvatar for image avatars)
- Loading states (use EtSkeleton separately)

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `EtSymbol` (main component)

```tsx
<EtSymbol
  size?: SymbolSize           // default: 'medium'
  shape?: SymbolShape         // default: 'rounded'
  backgroundColor?: string    // default: DEFAULT_SYMBOL_BG_COLOR ('#232733')
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
>
  {children}
</EtSymbol>
```

### `EtSymbol.Currency`

```tsx
<EtSymbol.Currency
  color?: string             // default: DEFAULT_SYMBOL_COLOR ('#FFFFFF')
>
  {children: string}          // Currency symbol text (e.g., "€", "$", "£", "A$")
</EtSymbol.Currency>
```

### `EtSymbol.Icon`

```tsx
<EtSymbol.Icon
  name: string               // EtIconV2 icon name (required)
  color?: string             // default: DEFAULT_SYMBOL_COLOR ('#FFFFFF')
/>
```

### `EtSymbol.Date`

```tsx
<EtSymbol.Date
  day: string                // "29"
  month: string              // "Apr"
  color?: string             // default: DEFAULT_SYMBOL_COLOR ('#FFFFFF')
/>
```

### `EtSymbol.Text`

```tsx
<EtSymbol.Text
  color?: string             // default: DEFAULT_SYMBOL_COLOR ('#FFFFFF')
>
  {children: string}          // Text to display (e.g., "PNG", "BTC")
</EtSymbol.Text>
```

### Types

| Type          | Values                               |
| ------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| `SymbolSize`  | `'small'` \| `'medium'` \| `'large'` |
| `SymbolShape` | `'rounded'` \| `'sharp'`             |

## Usage Patterns

### Currency symbol

```tsx
<EtSymbol backgroundColor="#005ca4">
  <EtSymbol.Currency>€</EtSymbol.Currency>
</EtSymbol>
```

### Icon

```tsx
<EtSymbol shape="sharp">
  <EtSymbol.Icon name="chat" />
</EtSymbol>
```

### Date

```tsx
<EtSymbol shape="sharp">
  <EtSymbol.Date day="29" month="Apr" />
</EtSymbol>
```

### Text label

```tsx
<EtSymbol>
  <EtSymbol.Text>PNG</EtSymbol.Text>
</EtSymbol>
```

### Different sizes and shapes

```tsx
<EtSymbol size="small" shape="sharp" backgroundColor="#037fd9">
  <EtSymbol.Currency>£</EtSymbol.Currency>
</EtSymbol>

<EtSymbol size="large" shape="rounded" backgroundColor="#00A44B">
  <EtSymbol.Currency>$</EtSymbol.Currency>
</EtSymbol>
```

## Anti-patterns

### Using subcomponents outside EtSymbol

```tsx
// BAD - will throw runtime error
<EtSymbol.Currency>€</EtSymbol.Currency>
<EtSymbol.Icon name="chat" />
<EtSymbol.Text>PNG</EtSymbol.Text>
```

**Fix:** Always wrap in `<EtSymbol>`.

## Architecture

### File Structure

```
libs/etoro-ui/src/components/data-display/symbol/
├── api/                     # Type definitions
├── constants.ts             # Shared constants (DEFAULT_SYMBOL_COLOR, DEFAULT_SYMBOL_BG_COLOR)
├── context/                 # SymbolContext for subcomponent communication
├── hooks/                   # useSymbolConfig - resolves size, borderRadius
├── subcomponents/           # Currency, Icon, Date, Text subcomponents
├── utils/                   # SIZE_CONFIGS, getBorderRadius, getSizeValue
├── et-symbol.tsx            # Main compound component
└── index.ts                 # Barrel exports
```

### Size Configurations

| Size   | Pixels | Rounded Radius | Sharp Radius | Currency Variant   | Text Variant            | Icon Size |
| ------ | ------ | -------------- | ------------ | ------------------ | ----------------------- | --------- |
| small  | 24px   | 4px (X1)       | 0px          | body-base-semibold | caption-regular         | 14px      |
| medium | 36px   | 8px (X2)       | 0px          | heading-large      | caption-medium          | 20px      |
| large  | 48px   | 8px (X2)       | 0px          | display-hero       | body-secondary-semibold | 24px      |

### Theme Colors

The component **does NOT apply currency colors automatically**. Currency theme colors are exposed via `useEtoroTheme` for consumers to manually pass into the `EtSymbol` `backgroundColor` prop:

- **`colors.eur`** - European Euro background color (blue)
- **`colors.usd`** - US Dollar background color (green)
- **`colors.gbp`** - British Pound background color (blue)
- **`colors.aud`** - Australian Dollar background color (dark blue)

**Example usage:**
```tsx
const { colors } = useEtoroTheme();

<EtSymbol backgroundColor={colors.eur}>
  <EtSymbol.Currency>€</EtSymbol.Currency>
</EtSymbol>
```

When `backgroundColor` is not provided, the component defaults to `DEFAULT_SYMBOL_BG_COLOR` (`#232733` - dark gray). The internal `EtSymbol.Currency` subcomponent renders the currency symbol text.

## Dependencies & Edges

### Internal Dependencies

- `useEtoroTheme` - provides overlay gradient colors
- `EtText` - text rendering for Currency, Date, and Text subcomponents
- `EtIconV2` - icon rendering for Icon subcomponent
- `SymbolContext` - React context for passing size info to subcomponents

### External Dependencies

- `expo-linear-gradient` - gradient overlay
- `react-native` - View, StyleSheet
